Status Code Description 200 OK. The input was classified. Also returned when the LLM failed: see Degraded Answers. 401 Unauthorized. Authentication is enabled and the token is missing, expired, wrongly signed, or has the wrong issuer or audience. 403 Forbidden. The token is valid but its client (<code>azp</code>) is not in <code>ALLOWED_CLIENTS</code>. 422 Unprocessable Entity. The request body failed validation: missing or blank <code>query</code>, <code>query</code> longer than 2000 characters, too many <code>history</code> items or <code>dataset_ids</code>, or a <code>dataset_ids</code> entry that is not a UUID. 500 Internal Server Error. An unexpected error occurred in the service. 503 Service Unavailable. The AAI signing keys could not be fetched, so the token could not be checked. Retry shortly. <p>Validation errors</p> <p>Request validation is handled by FastAPI and pydantic and returns <code>422</code> with a list of the offending fields:</p> <pre><code>{
  "detail": [
    {
      "type": "value_error",
      "loc": ["body", "query"],
      "msg": "Value error, query must not be blank",
      "input": "   "
    }
  ]
}
</code></pre>
